CloudBurrow patch 55 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1456). Needs 0047.

The bug: with a default time zone (patch 0047, BigQuery's project option
default_time_zone), a string literal the analyzer coerces to a TIMESTAMP
(ts > '2020-01-01 00:00:00', ts = '2019-12-31 22:00:00') was still read
in UTC: 0047 gave the zone to TIMESTAMP literals and casts written in the
text, but a coerced string is typed only by the analyzer, whose zone is
UTC (go-googlesql can build no other), and it folds the string into a
TIMESTAMP literal there. BigQuery reads it in the default zone ("if no
time zone is specified, the default time zone is used").

The patch gives the formatter the query text for a query with a default
zone, and a TIMESTAMP literal whose text in the query (its parse
location) is a quoted string with no zone is written as the TIMESTAMP of
its wall time in that zone. A string with a zone, a TIMESTAMP '...'
literal (0047's) and a query with no default zone are as before.
coerced_timestamp_literal_test.go has each form.

